// attention/ — attention mechanisms and the transformer blocks built on them.
//
// Sits on nn. Everything here is dense matrix arithmetic over a sequence:
// Q/K/V projections, scaled dot-product, softmax over the key axis, position
// encodings, the T5 relative-position bias, and the Pre-Norm block that stacks
// them.
//
// Two families live side by side because they share almost all of that.
// transformer_block is the ordinary one. sattention and spiking_attention
// replace softmax with fast_sigmoid_forward from surrogate.mbt (Zenke & Ganguli
// 2018) so a spike-emitting cell stays differentiable, and
// spiking_transformer_block is the Pre-Norm stack wired to those. Splitting
// spiking attention from vanilla would leave the two blocks with near-identical
// forward and backward passes and nothing but a different activation between
// them.
//
// `surrogate.mbt` itself stays in the root package. It is not attention -- it
// is the backward pass for a Heaviside spike, generally -- and srnn_demo.mbt
// needs it for a model that has nothing to do with attention here. The five
// call sites here reach it as `@snn_mbt.fast_sigmoid_forward` and
// `@snn_mbt.fast_sigmoid_surrogate`.
//
// rl/ is imported by patch_embedding.mbt, which builds its patch projection
// with a small MLP rather than a matrix multiply.
import {
  "riantr/snn_mbt/core",
  "riantr/snn_mbt/nn",
  "riantr/snn_mbt/activ",
  "riantr/snn_mbt/rl",
}
